US English speaker learning Mexican Spanish, A2, renting an apartment in Mexico City. Mexican vocabulary: "el departamento", "la renta", "el depósito", "los servicios"; "ustedes" for a group, never "vosotros", and a lesson aimed at a landlord would use "usted". Spain forms like "el piso", "el alquiler", "la fianza" or "los gastos" as the main word are wrong for this variant. Tips should target sounds English speakers get wrong (the tapped "r", pure vowels, "ll").